<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Max Frisch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1911–1991</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Max Frisch was a Swiss novelist, playwright and architect from Zurich. His novels Stiller and Homo Faber and his plays The Fire Raisers and Andorra examine questions of identity, guilt and conformity, and he was a sharp critic of Swiss complacency. He was one of the most widely read German-language writers of the post-war era.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/max-frisch.jpg" alt="Max Frisch" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Comet Photo AG (Zürich) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ETH-BIB-Max_Frisch-Com_C20-015-023-001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
